Package: pairedcountbrms
Title: Joint Bivariate-Count and Discrete-Difference brms Custom
    Families for Paired Counts
Version: 0.8.0
Date: 2026-08-03
Authors@R: person("Adam N. H.", "Smith", , "anhsmith@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides custom brms families for comparing two paired count
    sources. The principal families model the pair jointly, via trivariate
    reduction: a bivariate Poisson (bipois), its overdispersed bivariate
    Negative-Binomial sibling (binegbin), and a censoring-aware extension
    (binegbin_joint) that admits rows on which one of the two counts is
    unobserved, through its integrated-out marginal, and lets the two
    source-specific components differ in overdispersion. Modelling the pair
    rather than its difference captures the overall level, the correlation between
    sources, and marginal overdispersion alongside the disagreement, and
    supports simulating one count conditional on the other. An interpretable
    reparameterisation separates overall level, congruence, and source bias,
    giving each a finite null and so admitting penalised-complexity priors.
    Also provided are families that model the difference directly, for when
    only the disagreement is of interest or truncation via brms's resp_trunc()
    is required: the symmetric and asymmetric Skellam distributions (the
    distribution of the difference of two Poisson random variables), and
    discrete Laplace and discrete normal distributions discretised via CDF
    differencing, each with location fixed at zero or free, all sampled on a
    common SD-scale spread parameter.
